  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="types">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which type of shower is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">It depends on your hot water. An electric shower works in almost any home. A mixer needs good hot water pressure, and a power shower only suits a gravity system.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Shower</th><th>How it works</th><th>Best with</th><th>Fitted from</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Electric</strong></td><td>Heats cold mains water as it runs</td><td>Any system. Works when the boiler is off.</td><td>£375</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Bar mixer</strong></td><td>Mixes hot and cold, holds the set heat</td><td>Combi or unvented cylinder</td><td>£395</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Concealed mixer</strong></td><td>As a bar mixer, with the valve in the wall</td><td>Combi or unvented cylinder</td><td>£695</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Power shower</strong></td><td>Mixer with a pump inside</td><td>Gravity system only (tank in the loft)</td><td>£650</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Digital</strong></td><td>Set the exact heat on a pad or app</td><td>Most systems. Pumped models for gravity.</td><td>£850</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>Quick guide</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Want the lowest cost?</strong> An electric shower.</li>
        <li><strong>Have a combi boiler?</strong> A thermostatic mixer gives the best flow.</li>
        <li><strong>Weak flow and a tank in the loft?</strong> A power shower.</li>
        <li><strong>Doing up the whole bathroom?</strong> A concealed or digital shower looks neatest.</li>
        <li><strong>Young children or older people at home?</strong> Pick a thermostatic shower. It guards against scalding.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="water">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which shower suits my water system?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Look at how your home heats water. A shower that is wrong for your system will dribble, however good it is. We check this before we quote.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Combi boiler</h3>
          <p>No tank in the loft and no hot water cylinder. Hot water comes at mains pressure.</p>
          <p><strong>Fit:</strong> a thermostatic mixer or an electric shower.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Unvented cylinder</h3>
          <p>A sealed cylinder, often with no loft tank. It gives strong mains-pressure hot water.</p>
          <p><strong>Fit:</strong> any mixer, concealed or digital shower.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Gravity system</h3>
          <p>A cold water tank in the loft feeds a hot water cylinder. Pressure is often low.</p>
          <p><strong>Fit:</strong> a power shower, a pumped digital shower, or an electric shower.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Not sure?</h3>
          <p>Send us a photo of your boiler and airing cupboard. Or call and we will talk you through it.</p>
          <p><a href={TEL}>Call {PHONE}</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="brx-note" style="margin-top:1rem;"><p><strong>Power showers and combis do not mix.</strong> A power shower must only be fed from a tank and cylinder. It must never be connected to a combi boiler or the mains. If you want a stronger shower on a gravity system, a power shower or an <a href="/hot-water-cylinders-liverpool">unvented cylinder</a> is the answer.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="electric">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do I need an electrician for an electric shower?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Not for a like-for-like swap. If your shower needs a new circuit, our partner firm Ideal Electrical Solutions does the electrics.</p>
      <h3>Swapping an old electric shower</h3>
      <p>Most jobs are a straight swap. We check the cable, fuse and isolator suit the new shower. Then we fit it, test it and take the old one away. It usually takes 2 to 4 hours.</p>
      <h3>When you need an electrician</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>There has never been an electric shower in that spot.</li>
        <li>You want a bigger kW shower than the cable can take.</li>
        <li>The old circuit is not safe or is too small.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A new shower circuit is notifiable electrical work, so it must be done by a registered electrician. Our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk/showers">Ideal Electrical Solutions fits new electric shower circuits</a>. We book both trades together, so you only make one call.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a shower installation?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">The shower, the fitting, testing and taking the old one away. You get a fixed written price before we start.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>A new shower from a main brand, or fitting of one you have bought</li>
        <li>Removal of the old shower</li>
        <li>Hot and cold pipework connected, or the cold feed on an electric shower</li>
        <li>Riser rail, hose and head, or a fixed head on a concealed shower</li>
        <li>Seals checked around the tray or bath</li>
        <li>Full test for leaks, flow and temperature</li>
        <li>We show you how to use it and leave the instructions</li>
        <li>12-month workmanship guarantee, plus the maker's warranty</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not included: new tiling, moving the shower to a new wall, or a new electrical circuit. If you need any of these, we price them first.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does a shower installation work?</h2>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Call or send photos.</strong> Tell us what you have now and what you want. We can often price a swap from photos.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed price.</strong> For bigger jobs we visit for free. You get a written price before any work.</li>
        <li><strong>Fitting day.</strong> We turn off the water, protect the floor and take the old shower off.</li>
        <li><strong>The new shower goes in.</strong> A swap takes 2 to 4 hours. A concealed shower takes longer, as the pipes go into the wall.</li>
        <li><strong>Test and hand over.</strong> We check for leaks, set the heat and show you how it works. The old shower leaves with us.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Want a price for a new shower?</strong> Call and we will give you a fixed price.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="more-prices">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much do other shower jobs cost?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Fitting your own shower is from £195. A digital shower is from £850, and a bath to shower conversion is from £2,395. All prices include VAT.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Electric shower replaced, supplied and fitted</td><td>from £375</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Thermostatic bar mixer, supplied and fitted</td><td>from £395</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Power shower, supplied and fitted</td><td>from £650</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Concealed thermostatic shower, supplied and fitted</td><td>from £695</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Digital shower, supplied and fitted</td><td>from £850</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Fit a shower you have bought</td><td>from £195</td></tr>
            <tr><td><a href="/bathroom-fitters-liverpool">Bath to shower conversion</a></td><td>from £2,395</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Shower repairs</td><td>£120 first hour (weekdays 9am–4pm), £150 evenings, nights and weekends, £180 bank holidays</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>There is no call-out fee. If a repair runs past the first hour, we price the extra time before we carry on.</p>
      <p>Want a walk-in shower or a full new bathroom? See our <a href="/bathroom-fitters-liverpool">bathroom fitters in Liverpool</a>. Our team does the plumbing and the tiling.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="repair">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Should I repair or replace my shower?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Many faults can be fixed without a new shower. We look first and give you an honest answer before any work.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Hot then cold when a tap runs</h3>
          <p>The thermostatic cartridge is often worn. A new cartridge usually fixes it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Weak flow</h3>
          <p>Limescale in the head is the usual cause. If every tap is weak, it is the supply, not the shower.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Electric shower trips the power</h3>
          <p>Often a failed heater inside or water in the unit. It usually needs a new shower. Stop using it until it is checked.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Leaking valve or tray</h3>
          <p>A valve leak can often be fixed with a new seal or cartridge. A cracked tray must be replaced. Leaks can damage the ceiling below.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;">Electric showers often last 5 to 10 years. If yours is over 10 years old and has a fault, a new one is often better value. If water is coming through a ceiling, see our <a href="/leak-detection-liverpool">leak detection</a> page. For more faults and quick checks, see <a href="/shower-repair-liverpool">shower repair</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="brands">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which shower brands do you fit?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">We fit all the main brands. We can supply one for you, or fit one you have bought.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Good value</h3>
          <p>Triton and Bristan. Reliable, easy to get parts for, and good for rentals and second bathrooms.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Mid range</h3>
          <p>Mira and Aqualisa. The choice for most family homes. Electric, mixer and digital models.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Premium</h3>
          <p>Grohe, Hansgrohe, Vado and Crosswater. Brass bodies and the best finish. Rainfall and twin-head options.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Rainfall and twin heads</h3>
          <p>A large overhead head, often with a handset too. They work best on mains pressure or a pumped supply. We price them after a quick look.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
